# Sonrat Master System — binding rules

Follow `docs/PHASE0_ARCHITECTURE.md` and the MASTER SYSTEM PROMPT.

## Role
Principal architect + staff eng across backend, realtime, frontend, DevOps, security, QA. Build a **real multi-tenant production SaaS**, not a demo.

## V1 providers (behind abstractions only)
- AI: `AIProvider` → `GeminiProvider` (Gemini Live). No self-hosted LLM/GPU in V1.
- Telephony: `TelephonyProvider` → `ExotelProvider`. Capacity configurable, never hardcoded myths.
- Later: Sarvam/Local AI; other telephony — without rewriting Call Runtime.

## Planes (never mix)
Dashboard → API control plane only.
Realtime audio: Exotel → Voice Edge → Call Runtime → AI/Flow/Tools — never via API, Kafka, or Postgres.
Async: Kafka (events/work) → workers. Analytics: ClickHouse. Blobs: S3.

## Product modules
Organizations, Agents, Agent Flows, Sales/Campaigns, Customer Support, WhatsApp, Calls, Recordings, Analytics, Knowledge, Usage, Billing, Settings, Admin.

## Phase discipline
- Do NOT implement all phases at once.
- On `START PHASE N`: implement ONLY that phase.
- After each phase: report STATUS, files, DB, events, APIs, tests, issues, NEXT.
- STOP and fix if tests fail.
- Never say "production ready" without passing relevant tests.
- Do not blindly overwrite; inspect existing code; evolve toward target structure.

## Code quality
No god classes, no provider logic in domain, no hardcoded org workflows, no fake Gemini/Exotel success in production paths. Mocks for tests only.
